      "text": "To find the sum of \\(\\lfloor \\sqrt{k} \\rfloor\\) for \\(k\\) ranging from 1 to 16, we first need to understand the behavior of these floor functions for different integer values of \\(k\\).\n\n### Step-by-Step Breakdown\n\n1. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{1} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 1 \\rfloor = 1$**\n\n2. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 1.41... \\rfloor = 1$**\n\n3. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 1.73... \\rfloor = 1$**\n\n4. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{4} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2 \\rfloor = 2$**\n\n5. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{5} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.24... \\rfloor = 2$**\n\n6. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{6} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.44... \\rfloor = 2$**\n\n7. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{7} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.65... \\rfloor = 2$**\n\n8. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{8} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 2.83... \\rfloor = 2$**\n\n9. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{9} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3 \\rfloor = 3$**\n\n10. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{10} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.16... \\rfloor = 3$**\n\n11. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{11} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.32... \\rfloor = 3$**\n\n12. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{12} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.46... \\rfloor = 3$**\n\n13. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{13} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.61... \\rfloor = 3$**\n\n14. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{14} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.74... \\rfloor = 3$**\n\n15. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{15} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 3.87... \\rfloor = 3$**\n\n16. **$\\lfloor \\sqrt{16} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 4 \\rfloor = 4$**\n\nNext, we count the number of times each integer value from 2 to 4 appears:\n\n1. **Frequency of $2$:**\n   - $\\lfloor \\sqrt{k} \\rfloor = 2$ for $k = 4, 5, 6, \\ldots, 15$\n   - Total occurrences: \\(15 - 3 + 1 = 13\\) (since $4^2 = 16$ is excluded)\n   - Sum (\\(\\left\\lfloor \\sqrt{4} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\sqrt{5} \\right\\rfloor + \\cdots \\right\\rfloor\\)): \\(2 \\times 13 = 26\\)\n\n2. **Frequency of $3$:**\n   - $\\lfloor \\sqrt{k} \\rfloor = 3$ for $k = 9, 10, 11, \\ldots, 15$\n   - Total occurrences: \\(15 - 6 + 1 = 10\\) (since $6^2 = 36 > 16$ is excluded)\n   - Sum (\\(\\left\\lfloor \\sqrt{9} \\right\\rfloor + \\left\\lfloor \\sqrt{10} \\right\\rfloor + \\cdots \\right\\rfloor\\)): \\(3 \\times 10 = 30\\)\n\n3. **Frequency of $4$:**\n   - $\\lfloor \\sqrt{k} \\rfloor = 4$ for $k = 16$\n   - Total occurrence: \\(1\\) (since $16 = 4^2$)\n   - Sum (\\(\\left\\lfloor \\sqrt{16} \\right\\rfloor\\)): \\(4\\)\n\nNow, sum up all these values:\n\\[ 26 + 30 + 4 = 50 \\]\n\nThus, the final result is \\(\\boxed{50}\\).",
