      "text": "Since $\\lfloor \\sqrt{1} \\rfloor = \\lfloor 1 \\rfloor = 1,$ \\[\\lfloor \\sqrt{1} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor + \\cdots + \\lfloor \\sqrt{16} \\rfloor = 1 + \\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor + \\cdots + 3.\\]Next,  \\[\\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor + \\cdots + 3 = \\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor + \\ldots + \\lfloor \\sqrt{9} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{10} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{11} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{12} \\rfloor - 9.\\]We have  \\[\\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor + \\ldots + \\lfloor \\sqrt{9} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{10} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{11} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{12} \\rfloor = 1 + 2 + 2 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 4 = 16.\\]Therefore,  \\[1 + \\lfloor \\sqrt{2} \\rfloor + \\lfloor \\sqrt{3} \\rfloor + \\cdots + 3 = 1 + 16 - 9 = \\boxed{8}.\\]. The answer is 8",
